{"count":8,"findings":[{"category":"","description":"`set_pending_rewards` and `allocate` mutate global reward-backing state and per-owner unit balances without any `require_auth` or other caller restriction. If this module is ever exposed via public entrypoints (e.g., future integration/feature-flag mistakes), any account could (a) clear or set the `pending_rewards` gate to unblock/lock redemptions and alter funding mode checks, and/or (b) allocate unallocated units to arbitrary owners, manipulating reward distribution.

Exploit path (if exposed): attacker calls `set_pending_rewards(env, 0)` to bypass the “unsettled backing rewards” gate in `redeem_with`, then calls `allocate` to redirect units, affecting who can redeem backing value.

Current mitigations/limits: this module is behind `#[cfg(any(test, feature = "hybrid-rewards"))]` and `hybrid-rewards` hard-errors on `wasm32`, so it should be non-deployable in production builds; impact is therefore contingent on future changes or misconfiguration.","file_path":"peridot-contracts/contracts/receipt-vault/src/reward_backing.rs","id":"84ddb218-8244-47e0-b0de-21fc58a075ff","impacted_code":"pub fn set_pending_rewards(env: &Env, count: u32) {
