    env.storage().persistent().set(&key, &value);
    env.storage()
        .persistent()
        .extend_ttl(&key, TTL_LOW, TTL_HIGH);
}","line_end":215,"line_start":197,"recommendation":"If this becomes on-chain callable, restrict allocation to an authorized coordinator and/or enforce limits (e.g., only allow allocating to addresses present in a verified epoch ledger, or require nonzero allocations only for known participants). Consider deleting owner keys when balance reaches zero (if consistent with desired accounting invariants).","repo":"https://github.com/PeridotFinance/Peridot-Soroban","severity":"LOW","sha":"95c6e39bd1095d43cd4240b8ce7d8d1d82044aba","state":"OPEN","title":"Unbounded persistent owner records can be created"},{"category":"","description":"Several security-relevant configuration flags are stored in **instance storage** (`MinCashReserveBps`, `ClCustody`, `ClCustodyContext`, `CashBorrowingEnabled`), but this module never bumps instance-storage TTLs (no `env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(...)` anywhere). In Soroban, instance entries can expire independently of persistent entries; once expired, reads fall back to defaults (`None` / `false`).

If the contract relies on these flags for safety properties, their expiry can silently change market behavior without admin action. A concrete example is `ClCustody` (custody-only market mode): `deposit_into_boosted` explicitly forbids boosted-vault interaction when `cl_custody` is true, but if `ClCustody` expires it will read as `false` and the contract may start executing non-custody code paths for a custody-configured market, potentially moving assets into a boosted vault or enabling flows that were meant to be permanently disabled for custody markets.

Because this is a time-based state-loss vector that can flip critical configuration, it can lead to fund-loss or broken accounting once the instance TTL is reached, and can be triggered simply by letting the market sit idle past TTL (no attacker privileges required).","file_path":"peridot-contracts/contracts/receipt-vault/src/storage.rs","id":"bc0b2371-07ca-4cf5-9d54-48ae146a1c1d","impacted_code":"pub enum DataKey {
