}","line_end":283,"line_start":4,"recommendation":"Add explicit instance TTL maintenance for any instance keys that must persist for the contract lifetime (e.g., a `bump_instance_ttl(env)` helper called by `ensure_initialized` and any other frequent entrypoints), or move these configuration flags to persistent storage if they are intended to be durable. Ensure any custody-mode invariants cannot be silently disabled by missing instance state.","repo":"https://github.com/PeridotFinance/Peridot-Soroban","severity":"MEDIUM","sha":"95c6e39bd1095d43cd4240b8ce7d8d1d82044aba","state":"OPEN","title":"Instance config flags can expire and disable safeguards"},{"category":"","description":"`settle_one_recycled` and `compound` perform external swaps via `strategy.hybrid_swap` with `minimum` hardcoded to `1`, meaning any caller can trigger reward-token conversion at arbitrarily bad execution prices (including during manipulated AMM conditions). If this module were ever enabled in a deployable WASM build (e.g., by removing the current `compile_error!` gate for `hybrid-rewards` on `wasm32`), an attacker could front-run/back-run the permissionless `recycle`/`compound` flows to force conversions at extreme slippage, effectively extracting value from protocol rewards into the AMM and reducing rewards for all holders.

Note: In the current repository configuration, `reward_settlement` is only compiled for tests or non-wasm builds (`#[cfg(any(test, feature = "hybrid-rewards"))]`), and `hybrid-rewards` is explicitly blocked on `wasm32` (`compile_error!` in `src/lib.rs`). So this is not exploitable in the deployed ReceiptVault as-is, but is a high-risk footgun if the feature gate is changed.","file_path":"peridot-contracts/contracts/receipt-vault/src/reward_settlement.rs","id":"d4d748d9-478a-49f1-9b40-49081de0aeb5","impacted_code":"fn settle_one_recycled(env: &Env, asset: &Address) -> Outcome {
