}","line_end":140,"line_start":118,"recommendation":"If this code is ever deployed, require `owner.require_auth()` (or equivalent strong authorization) before persisting any per-owner accounting, and/or avoid creating/persisting ledger accounts when `weight == 0` and no state existed previously. Consider explicit bounds/allowlists on who can trigger allocation for third parties.","repo":"https://github.com/PeridotFinance/Peridot-Soroban","severity":"LOW","sha":"95c6e39bd1095d43cd4240b8ce7d8d1d82044aba","state":"OPEN","title":"Arbitrary owner parameter can bloat ledger storage"},{"category":"","description":"`utilization()` returns `0` when `denom == 0` (i.e., `cash + borrows == reserves`), which represents a 100% reserve share / undefined utilization edge case. Returning 0 makes `get_borrow_rate` fall back to ~`base_rate`, dramatically *lowering* rates exactly when the pool is most stressed.

Exploit path (economic): if protocol state can reach `pooled_reserves == cash + borrows` (e.g., large accumulated reserves/admin fees plus cash drained via withdrawals while borrows remain), subsequent interest accrual in `ReceiptVault::update_interest` that queries this model will compute a near-minimum borrow rate, undercharging borrowers and harming lenders/protocol accounting until the condition clears.","file_path":"peridot-contracts/contracts/jump-rate-model/src/lib.rs","id":"379b2c5f-5db6-421c-a9db-3ecbbea105b0","impacted_code":"fn utilization(cash: u128, borrows: u128, reserves: u128) -> u128 {
